   "html_text": "Without objecting to this account of the semantics of names of SQs, we can add that the doctrine of SQs solves an epistemic problem arising from Locke’s thesis that the limited knowledge we have is sufficient for our needs (E 1.5). The solution to this problem is in part about the world. Jacovides overlooks Locke’s semantic theory of simple ideas of sensation in general and its function in his epistemology. The key texts are Essay 2.30.1–2, 2.31.1–2. and 4.4.4. In outline, God sustains steady ca",
